Subject: Guard buffer-underflow reads on empty paths and strings in SPL, INI, open_basedir, phar, sqlite3, and strip_tags
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: Under Fil-C, evaluating IS_SLASH_AT(buf, len - 1) or buf[len - 1] when len is 0 triggers a deterministic ptr < lower panic. In ext/spl/spl_directory.c, spl_filesystem_info_set_filename() evaluated IS_SLASH_AT(intern->file_name, intern->file_name_len - 1) before checking intern->file_name_len > 1, panicking on new SplFileInfo(''). Backport upstream php/php-src commit 9f9ee0186eb3d1fcc2b3a4ecc55a0195233fd670 ("Fix memory error in spl_directory.c", landed in PHP 7.0), commit 7ec8b8d49f42e6edf520324b202c5754cd6d9e90 (main/php_ini.c php_load_zend_extension_cb), and the PHP 7.4 p >= buf + 1 guards in ext/standard/string.c php_strip_tags_ex(), and add matching non-empty length guards to the remaining [len - 1] path sites audited in main/fopen_wrappers.c, main/php_open_temporary_file.c, ext/phar/phar_object.c, and ext/sqlite3/sqlite3.c.
Upstream-Status: Backport (php/php-src commits 9f9ee0186eb3d1fcc2b3a4ecc55a0195233fd670 and 7ec8b8d49f42e6edf520324b202c5754cd6d9e90, PHP 7.4 ext/standard/string.c, plus local matching [len-1] bounds guards)
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: none
Origin-Kind: backport
Origin-Project: php/php-src
Origin-Commit: 9f9ee0186eb3d1fcc2b3a4ecc55a0195233fd670
Origin-URL: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/9f9ee0186eb3d1fcc2b3a4ecc55a0195233fd670

